WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.195
How does floodwater become an economic loss? Connect water depth,

00:00:05.575 --> 00:00:08.920
damage to individual objects, and the cost for a building

00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:13.220
and its contents. Explore a one-story home, a two-story home,

00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:17.620
or a clinic. Rotate, zoom, and use the cutaway to

00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:21.370
examine objects at different heights. Change the water level with

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:25.920
a slider or the indoor-depth presets. Red shading reveals modeled

00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:30.583
damage, while the receipt separates contents from building components. Select

00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:34.295
an item to see its value, damage percentage, and cost.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.832
The chart displays percentages or dollars, showing how individual losses

00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:41.870
add up. Raise a selected item to test how its

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.820
loss changes at the same water level. The interactive guide

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:50.058
helps you find each control. These are illustrative classroom estimates.

00:00:50.312 --> 00:00:54.070
Your challenge: explain why the same flood does not cause

00:00:53.962 --> 00:00:55.820
the same damage everywhere.
